WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
John, Chapter Twenty.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:10.800
The first day of the week cometh Mary Magdalene early, when it was yet dark, unto the sepulchre, and seeth the stone taken away from the sepulchre.

3
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:22.400
Then she runneth, and cometh to Simon Peter, and to the other disciple, whom Jesus loved, and saith unto them, They have taken away the Lord out of the sepulchre, and we know not where they have laid him.

4
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.800
Peter therefore went forth, and that other disciple, and came to the sepulchre.

5
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.933
So they ran both together: and the other disciple did outrun Peter, and came first to the sepulchre.

6
00:00:32.933 --> 00:00:38.800
And he stooping down, and looking in, saw the linen clothes lying; yet went he not in.

7
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:52.267
Then cometh Simon Peter following him, and went into the sepulchre, and seeth the linen clothes lie, And the napkin, that was about his head, not lying with the linen clothes, but wrapped together in a place by itself.

8
00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:59.067
Then went in also that other disciple, which came first to the sepulchre, and he saw, and believed.

9
00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:03.333
For as yet they knew not the scripture, that he must rise again from the dead.

10
00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:07.333
Then the disciples went away again unto their own home.

11
00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:22.000
But Mary stood without at the sepulchre weeping: and as she wept, she stooped down, and looked into the sepulchre, And seeth two angels in white sitting, the one at the head, and the other at the feet, where the body of Jesus had lain.

12
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.600
And they say unto her, Woman, why weepest thou?

13
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:31.200
She saith unto them, Because they have taken away my Lord, and I know not where they have laid him.

14
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:38.000
And when she had thus said, she turned herself back, and saw Jesus standing, and knew not that it was Jesus.

15
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.867
Jesus saith unto her, Woman, why weepest thou?

16
00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:43.067
whom seekest thou?

17
00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:52.400
She, supposing him to be the gardener, saith unto him, Sir, if thou have borne him hence, tell me where thou hast laid him, and I will take him away.

18
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.533
Jesus saith unto her, Mary.

19
00:01:54.533 --> 00:01:59.067
She turned herself, and saith unto him, Rabboni; which is to say, Master.

20
00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:10.533
Jesus saith unto her, Touch me not; for I am not yet ascended to my Father: but go to my brethren, and say unto them, I ascend unto my Father, and your Father; and to my God, and your God.

21
00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:16.800
Mary Magdalene came and told the disciples that she had seen the Lord, and that he had spoken these things unto her.

22
00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:28.933
Then the same day at evening, being the first day of the week, when the doors were shut where the disciples were assembled for fear of the Jews, came Jesus and stood in the midst, and saith unto them, Peace be unto you.

23
00:02:28.933 --> 00:02:33.200
And when he had so said, he shewed unto them his hands and his side.

24
00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.000
Then were the disciples glad, when they saw the Lord.

25
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:42.667
Then said Jesus to them again, Peace be unto you: as my Father hath sent me, even so send I you.

26
00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:57.200
And when he had said this, he breathed on them, and saith unto them, Receive ye the Holy Ghost: Whose soever sins ye remit, they are remitted unto them; and whose soever sins ye retain, they are retained.

27
00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:01.600
But Thomas, one of the twelve, called Didymus, was not with them when Jesus came.

28
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:06.533
The other disciples therefore said unto him, We have seen the Lord.

29
00:03:06.533 --> 00:03:17.733
But he said unto them, Except I shall see in his hands the print of the nails, and put my finger into the print of the nails, and thrust my hand into his side, I will not believe.

30
00:03:17.733 --> 00:03:27.733
And after eight days again his disciples were within, and Thomas with them: then came Jesus, the doors being shut, and stood in the midst, and said, Peace be unto you.

31
00:03:27.733 --> 00:03:39.600
Then saith he to Thomas, Reach hither thy finger, and behold my hands; and reach hither thy hand, and thrust it into my side: and be not faithless, but believing.

32
00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:44.000
And Thomas answered and said unto him, My Lord and my God.

33
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:51.600
Jesus saith unto him, Thomas, because thou hast seen me, thou hast believed: blessed are they that have not seen, and yet have believed.

34
00:03:51.600 --> 00:04:05.600
And many other signs truly did Jesus in the presence of his disciples, which are not written in this book: But these are written, that ye might believe that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God; and that believing ye might have life through his name.

